[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Every scribe call and every render pays a full graph load

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[EVIDENCE]
UID: EV-SCRIBE-LOAD-COST
TITLE: Every scribe call and every render pays a full graph load
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
SOURCE: strictdoc-trial worktree, 348-node canon, warm cache; strictdoc 0.28.3; 2026-08-31
STATEMENT: >>>
Measured in the strictdoc-trial worktree against a 348-node canon, warm, each
command confirmed to exit 0 with non-empty output before its timing was read:

    scribe show <uid>     1.05 s     one graph load
    scribe check          1.56 s     one graph load
    strictdoc export      1.76 s     one load, 10.3 MB index.json
    wireline.py           0.19 s     given that index.json
    python startup        0.017 s

scribe new pays THREE loads -- the command's own, a reload to resolve the
grammar alias on the new document, and verify's reload to prove the written
bytes still parse -- measured at 1.96 s under --dry-run, which skips only the
third. So authoring ten nodes costs about 30 seconds of graph loading.

A cold number could not be taken: STRICTDOC_CACHE_DIR asserts its value equals
the literal Output/_cache, so redirecting it raises rather than loading. A
first attempt read 0.42 s and was a traceback, not a load.
<<<
